This is an excerpt from an email by Steve Jobs. Write down its last line that we omitted in the handout.
! Sent from my iPad [accept Sent from my iPhone].
/ in his email, Jobs lists a variety of things that he uses even though he did not create them. However, he did create the gadget from which he sent his letter. Sent from my iPhone/Sent from my iPad is the standard signature automatically added by the iOS email client, but in this email, it gained symbolic significance.
^ https://stevejobsarchive.com/
@ Eugene Mirotin

? When the player talks to a certain character in one video game, the program scans the memory of the player's console looking for save files from other games. The purpose of this is to demonstrate the ability of this character to… do what?
! read minds.
/ during the dialogue, the program of Metal Gear Solid finds save files from other games, so the boss called Psycho Mantis might say something like: “You like Castlevania, don’t you?”
^ https://metalgear.fandom.com/wiki/Psycho_Mantis
@ Eugene Mirotin

? In one movie, a convict exercises his right to order an expensive dinner into his cell and then uses the remains of the food as a weapon. The dish that he ordered is named after a letter. What letter?
! T.
/ the T-shaped bone that gave name to the T-bone steak has a fitting shape to be used as a melee weapon. An actual weapon of the same shape is called the push dagger.
^ Law Abiding Citizen
@ Eugene Mirotin

? [When reading the question out loud, do not indicate different capitalization; when displaying the question on screen, decapitalize all words “first” and “second”.]
In one Chinese recipe, when an egg is poured over the cooking rice, it is metaphorically called FIRST over SECOND. FIRST is given for the first, and SECOND, for the second. Name FIRST or SECOND.
! gold [accept silver]
/ an egg yolk over white rice is metaphorically compared to gold on silver. In all kinds of contests, gold is traditionally awarded for the first place, and silver, for the second place.
^ https://asianfoodnetwork.com/en/videos/series/destination-flavour-china/yang-zhou-fried-rice.html#:~:text=Gold over silver, is where,in little pieces of egg
